course: dictionary
lesson: 9945
title: A tiny primate with huge eyes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dictionary entry gives you the meaning of a word, and the sentences around it give you clues. The first meaning says a tarsier is a tiny primate from islands such as the Philippines and Borneo. A primate is a group of animals that includes monkeys, apes and humans.
explain: Look at the context clues. «Tarsiers are tiny primates whose each eye is about as big as their brain.» The eyes are described as huge, so you can picture a tarsier with very large eyes. Always check your idea by putting it back into the sentence.
explain: In science, the words work together to explain how an animal lives. A tarsier is nocturnal, so its huge eyes help it see at night. Turning its head almost all the way round helps it look around in the dark, a little like an owl.
fact: A tarsier is a tiny primate from islands in South-East Asia, such as the Philippines and Borneo.
fact: Each tarsier eye is about as big as its brain.
fact: A tarsier has huge round eyes, long back legs and a long thin tail.
fact: «Nocturnal» means active at night.
fact: Some kinds of tarsier are endangered because their forests are cut down.
exercise: What is a tarsier? | A plant with long roots | A large bird that cannot fly | *A tiny primate from islands in South-East Asia | A fish that lives in deep seas
exercise: Which body part is about as big as a tarsier's brain? | Back legs | Tail | *Each eye | Ears
exercise: Why might a tarsier's huge eyes help it? | It has no other way to find food | Its eyes are small and it cannot see well | *It is nocturnal, so its eyes help it see at night | It lives underwater and needs eyes that can swim
test: Which phrase describes how a tarsier moves its head? | *It keeps its head still and turns its body | It can turn its head almost all the way round | It can only nod its head up and down | It has no neck at all
test: Which word means active at night? | Tiny | Primate | *Nocturnal | Endangered
exam: Some kinds of tarsier are endangered. What does endangered most likely mean? | Very happy and full of energy | *At risk of dying out | Found in every country in the world | Good at swimming and diving
